data.content:
Done. Here's what was added:

**`Clock.cs`** — a static ambient context using `AsyncLocal<T>` so parallel tests don't interfere:

```csharp
Clock.UtcNow              // use in production code (replaces DateTimeOffset.UtcNow)
```

**In tests**, pin the time with a disposable scope:

```csharp
var due = new DateTimeOffset(2026, 7, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero);
using (Clock.Override(due.AddDays(-1)))
{
    Assert.False(new InvoiceCalculator().IsOverdue(due));
}
using (Clock.Override(due.AddDays(1)))
{
    Assert.True(new InvoiceCalculator().IsOverdue(due));
}
```

**Why this is the lightest option:**
- No DI container needed
- One null-check per call in production (essentially free)
- `AsyncLocal` keeps parallel/xUnit tests isolated
- Dispose resets automatically — no cleanup pollution
